  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Puck carrying – 2-on-2 with four nets",
  "description": "Play 2-on-2 in an area of about 20 × 10 metres with two small nets at each end. Both teams may score in all four nets. Split the rink across its width, so each area is long enough to skate with the puck and attack the space behind the opponents. The diagram shows two areas, one in each half of the rink, and is not to scale.\n\nIf you don't have four small nets, use cones. If you use full-size nets without goalies, the defenders have to pressure much harder; an extra rule can then be that you may not shoot while an opponent stands in front of you with the net behind them – you have to skate past first.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Carry the puck into the free space – speed up once you are past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "If one net is closed off, change direction and go for another."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence: when is it hard to defend? Talk it through with the players."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When can you take one hand off the stick to protect the puck or reach further?"
    }
  ],
